# TRIM-backed recycling + EIRENE absorb-and-re-emit for D on a C wall (DIII-D).
#
# Channels evaluated in order; first to cross U~U[0,1] fires.
#  1) T ...  probability = R_N from TRIM table (reflected as same species)
#  2) A R f  absorb-and-re-emit; R = wall recycling fraction,
#            f = atom->molecule partition (fraction of returned atoms that
#            come back as D2; default EIRENE/WTD = 0.95).
#
# Wall material: C (graphite targets + stainless chamber, approximated as C).

# D+ recycling: neutralize + TRIM reflect as D, else absorb-and-re-emit as
# 95% D2 / 5% D.
D+ --> D
T D_on_C

D+ --> D2
A 0.99 0.95

# D recycling: identical pipeline for atomic D.
D --> D
T D_on_C

D --> D2
A 0.99 0.95

# D2 recycling: no molecular-reflection table; simple absorb-and-return.
D2 --> D2
A 0.99
